      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nint main() {\n\tint n, s;\n\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\n\tassert(s > 0 && s < n && n < 8000);\n\n\t// Flatten matrix into a contiguous 1D array for spatial locality\n\tstd::vector<int> mat(n * n);\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\n\t\t\tscanf(\"%d\", &mat[i * n + j]);\n\n\t// Build integral image in one pass over mat, avoiding intermediate H storage.\n\t// Use a temporary row prefix buffer to compute each row's cumulative sums,\n\t// then add them to the previous II row. This reduces memory traffic by\n\t// eliminating writes/reads of the full H matrix.\n\tstd::vector<long long> II((n + 1) * (n + 1), 0);\n\tstd::vector<long long> row_prefix(n + 1, 0); // reusable per-row prefix buffer\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n\t\t// Compute prefix sums for this row of mat\n\t\trow_prefix[0] = 0;\n\t\tfor (int j = 1; j <= n; ++j)\n\t\t\trow_prefix[j] = row_prefix[j - 1] + mat[i * n + j - 1];\n\n\t\t// Combine with previous II row to produce current II row\n\t\tlong long* prev_row = &II[(i)     * (n + 1)];\n\t\tlong long* curr_row = &II[(i + 1) * (n + 1)];\n\t\tcurr_row[0] = 0;\n\t\tfor (int j = 1; j <= n; ++j)\n\t\t\tcurr_row[j] = prev_row[j] + row_prefix[j];\n\t}\n\n\t// Search for maximum SxS submatrix sum using integral image.\n\t// Apply two-dimensional tiling with a smaller block size (32) to improve\n\t// temporal reuse of II rows within L1 cache. Each tile touches only B columns\n\t// from the two active rows, reducing working set per iteration.\n\tconst int B = 32;\n\tlong long mxSum = -2147483648LL;\n\tfor (int i0 = 0; i0 <= n - s; i0 += B) {\n\t\tint imax = std::min(i0 + B, n - s + 1);\n\t\tfor (int j0 = 0; j0 <= n - s; j0 += B) {\n\t\t\tint jmax = std::min(j0 + B, n - s + 1);\n\t\t\tfor (int i = i0; i < imax; ++i) {\n\t\t\t\tconst long long* row_i   = &II[i * (n + 1)];\n\t\t\t\tconst long long* row_is  = &II[(i + s) * (n + 1)];\n\t\t\t\tfor (int j = j0; j < jmax; ++j) {\n\t\t\t\t\tlong long sub_sum = row_is[j + s] - row_i[j + s] - row_is[j] + row_i[j];\n\t\t\t\t\tif (sub_sum > mxSum)\n\t\t\t\t\t\tmxSum = sub_sum;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tprintf(\"%d\\n\", static_cast<int>(mxSum));\n\treturn 0;\n}",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Eliminating the intermediate H matrix by computing the integral image in a single pass over mat reduces memory traffic (fewer writes and reads), improving cache efficiency. Reducing the tile size from 64 to 32 shrinks the working set of active II rows per inner loop, increasing L1 data reuse during the search phase.",
  "notes": "Combined two improvements: (1) removed H storage by computing row prefix sums on-the-fly and directly updating II; (2) decreased block size B from 64 to 32 for better temporal locality. Both changes target memory bandwidth reduction and cache utilization without altering correctness.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "eliminate intermediate H matrix by integrating row prefix accumulation into the integral image construction loop",
    "reduce two-dimensional tile size from 64 to 32 for improved L1 reuse"
  ]
